    "leafs": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Maple Leafs",
      "league": "NHL",
      "record": "32-36-14",
      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season didn't end with a flourish; it ended with a thud, and the number that sticks is the same one that has haunted this club all spring: 78 points, 31 games behind, eighth in the Atlantic and buried at 15th overall with a 32-36-14 record. <strong>That's the headline now - not a chase, but a cleanup job.</strong> There are no more masks to wear here, no soft-pedaled excuses about a bounce or a bad night. A seven-game skid finished the body of work, and it left the Leafs looking less like a team that underachieved than one that never found a stable identity. The offseason questions are the real story: whether the coaching seat needs a reset, which veterans still fit, and how much patience remains for a core that could not drag this season back from the edge. The front office has decisions on free agency, the draft, and whether to keep patching holes or finally tear down to the studs. <strong>What matters next is whether Toronto chooses another quick fix - or finally makes the hard, clean break this mess now demands.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated June 9, 2026"
      },
