    "raptors": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Raptors",
      "league": "NBA",
      "record": "46-36",
      "detail": "3rd in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "Momentum has a way of turning a playoff series into a knife fight, and Toronto has dragged Cleveland into one. <strong>The Raptors and Cavaliers are knotted 2-2 after four games</strong> - a fitting scoreline for a team that finished 46-36, sat third in the Atlantic, and earned the No. 5 seed by being tough enough to survive but not yet clean enough to coast. The last 48 hours have only sharpened the edge around this matchup, because now every possession carries weight and every mistake gets replayed in the film room like an indictment. Toronto's story remains the same and it is no small one: the stars have to be steady, the supporting cast has to hit open looks, and the defense has to survive the first punch. The record says respectable; the series says unfinished. That is the whole truth of a team with W1 on the ledger and the season's real test still in front of it. <strong>The next swing game looms with the series tied 2-2, and Toronto has to seize it before Cleveland does</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated June 9, 2026"
      },
